Force alwayslink=1 by default in grpc_cc_library, so static initializers
in cc files (e.g. _GLOBAL__sub_I_client_context.cc that sets
grpc::g_client_callbacks) are preserved when grpc is statically linked
into a Rust binary (netsim, casimir). Without this, the rules_rust link
step drops .init_array entries from .o files that have no symbol pulled
in directly by Rust, and ClientContext::ClientContext crashes at runtime
with a NULL g_client_callbacks dereference on riscv64.
---
diff --git a/bazel/grpc_build_system.bzl b/bazel/grpc_build_system.bzl
--- a/bazel/grpc_build_system.bzl
+++ b/bazel/grpc_build_system.bzl
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ def grpc_cc_library(
         standalone = False,  # @unused
         testonly = False,
         visibility = None,
-        alwayslink = 0,
+        alwayslink = 1,
         data = [],
         tags = [],
         linkopts = [],
